---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Container from '../Container.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../SectionHeader.astro';
import HeartSignalButton from '../HeartSignalButton.astro';
import galacticMonkPhoto from '../../assets/roster-galactic-monk.jpg';
import sarahStarrPhoto from '../../assets/roster-sarah-starr.jpg';

/*
  Pitch page section 7 — who (docs/pitch-demo-sitemap.md §4.7 + §4.8, merged).

  FOUNDERS CARD, AND THE "THE ROSTER" REGISTER HEADING/INTRO, REMOVED
  (2026-09-10, owner request). The section originally merged two labelled
  registers per `creative-director` REVIEW FIX 5 — founders full width, roster
  beneath, each under its own <h3> — because two adjacent people-sections with
  no confirmed names in either read as padding. With founders gone, a lone
  "The roster" label was redundant next to the section's own "Current roster"
  kicker, so the owner had that removed too, along with its lorem-ipsum intro
  paragraph. The individual roster placeholder cards below are unchanged — the
  owner was explicit those stay. If founders come back, re-read that review fix
  before re-adding a second labelled register.

  REVIEW FIX 4 — NO "CONVERSATIONS IN PROGRESS" VAPOR. Originally: no invented
  names, no bios, no portraits, no follower or audience figures (banned even
  when real), no "in conversation with" implying a commitment that does not
  exist — each card was a role in the network's own language, a dashed
  placeholder frame, and Latin where the words would go. Cards 1 and 2 now
  carry real, consent-confirmed names/roles/links (below), which this fix
  never banned — it banned invention, not disclosure once consent exists.

  PORTRAIT BAN OVERRIDDEN FOR CARDS 1 AND 2 (2026-09-10, owner request,
  flagged before applying each time). The "no portraits, banned even when
  real" line above was read back to the owner explicitly for each photo
  before it went in; they confirmed both are genuine, rights-cleared photos
  of the real people, used with consent, and asked for the ban lifted
  card-by-card. Don't assume this override is a standing policy for future
  roster additions — get the same confirmation per photo, per person. Card
  1's photo was swapped once already (galacticmonk.com headshot →
  "monk-beach.jpg"); card 2's photo was swapped once too, after a portrait-
  shaped first attempt produced a bad crop (see COPY STATUS) — the
  ban-override confirmation applies to whichever image is currently wired in,
  not to a specific file; re-confirm again if either changes again. Re-review
  with `creative-director`: this section now has one
  placeholder card and two named-linked-and-photographed cards, which the
  dashed --border-placeholder frame (still applied to all three, see .card
  below) no longer honestly describes for cards 1 and 2.

  BIO LINE AND "ROOM THEY LEAD" REMOVED (2026-09-10, owner request). Every
  card used to carry a lorem-ipsum bio sentence and a labelled "room they
  lead" line. Removed entirely, not just for the two named cards — the owner
  didn't want lorem ipsum sitting next to real names, and cutting it only for
  cards 1–2 would have left the placeholder card in a different shape from the
  rest.

  PLACEHOLDER CARD SIMPLIFIED TO "SLOT PENDING" (2026-09-10, owner request).
  The third card no longer uses the "Placeholder" tag + "Name" + role
  scaffold — it's a named person or it just says "Slot pending," nothing
  else. `RosterEntry.role` is optional now for this reason; a card branches
  entirely on whether `name` is set (see the template below), so a named
  card is: photo (if any), name, role, website icon-link (if any); an
  unnamed one is an avatar and the one line of text.

  AVATAR ADDED FOR THE PENDING SLOT (2026-09-10, owner request), so the
  unfilled card keeps the same circle-then-text shape as the two filled ones
  instead of leaving a gap where a photo would be. Iterated same-day: a "?"
  glyph → public/anon.svg (a generic person-with-"?" glyph reads more like an
  avatar placeholder than a bare question mark), and the circle fill went
  from neutral --color-bg-elevated → --color-electric-pink → OfferingCard's
  card gradient, copied verbatim to visually match the offering cards. Full
  reasoning for the current state is on `.pending-avatar` in the styles
  below, including why that gradient is copied rather than tokenized.

  HEADING (2026-09-11, owner-confirmed): "Influencer talent list to be updated as
  prospects verify interest." Reads close to the "conversations in
  progress" pattern this fix bans, so it was flagged and the owner confirmed
  before it went in: there are real, current prospects being asked to verify
  interest, not an invented pipeline. If that stops being true, this heading
  needs to change with it.

  ROSTER GROWN TO FIVE CARDS (2026-09-10, owner request) — two more "Slot
  pending" cards added alongside the original one, so the row now holds two
  named people and three pending slots. Doesn't change or resolve the DATA
  GAP or the "no invented roster" standard below: three unnamed cards are
  exactly as honest as one was, just a wider row. See the FIVE-CARD ROW
  comment in the styles below for how the grid was reworked to fit them.

  Two additional five-card rows of pending slots added at the owner's request,
  then a fourth row (2026-09-11, same request pattern). The roster now
  contains two named people and eighteen pending slots.

  DATA GAP (owner) — BLOCKING for the pending cards: name, what
  they make or lead, naming consent, and whether a cleared portrait exists,
  per person. Cards 1 (Galactic Monk, Wayshower/Alchemist/Producer) and 2
  (Sarah Starr, Galactic Guide, Space Weather, & Astrology) have confirmed
  names, roles, naming consent, and a personal-site link and cleared portrait
  each.

  COPY STATUS: cards 1 and 2's names, roles, links, and photos are real,
  owner-supplied and consent-confirmed (2026-09-10) — src/assets/roster-
  galactic-monk.jpg and src/assets/roster-sarah-starr.jpg. The
  remaining cards' "Slot pending" text is the field left to fill on each,
  left visible on purpose so a reviewer can see exactly what is missing
  rather than what is asserted.

  DOMAIN TEXT REPLACED WITH A WEBSITE ICON-LINK (2026-09-10, owner request).
  Cards 1 and 2 used to spell out the URL as visible link text; that's gone,
  replaced by public/website.svg as an icon-only link (`.card-link` /
  `.card-link-icon` below), same CSS-mask technique as the pending avatar and
  OfferingCard.astro's icons. The link's accessible name comes from
  `aria-label="{name}'s website"` on the `<a>`, not from visible text — check
  that stays true if this ever changes to more than two people having a URL,
  a `<span class="sr-only">` fallback is the usual pattern if `aria-label`
  ever feels insufficient (e.g. if the icon needs a visible tooltip too).

  "INTERESTED" BADGE ADDED TO CARDS 1 AND 2 (2026-09-10, owner request) —
  public/check.svg plus the word, in a pill on the avatar's corner (same
  pattern as CityCard.astro's "Launching" badge). `RosterEntry.interested` is
  a boolean set per-person rather than inferred from having a photo, so it
  stays a deliberate owner claim, not a side effect of some other field being
  filled in. This is a status about the two confirmed people, not a new
  roster-size claim — doesn't touch the DATA GAP or REVIEW FIX 4 above.

  SARAH STARR'S PHOTO WAS REPLACED (2026-09-10). The first version was a
  704x920 portrait-shaped photo; fit into a square thumbnail, it left too
  much shoulder/chest below the chin, and a same-day attempt to fix that by
  biasing the crop (Astro Image `position` prop, then a manually pre-cropped
  source file) still read as off-center once masked into a circle, because a
  non-square source has no horizontal crop slack for Sharp to redistribute —
  full width always shows, so an asymmetric hairstyle reads as "leaning" no
  matter what position keyword is used. Replaced with
  "assets/sarah-starr-profile.jpg" (owner-supplied), which is natively square
  (1080x1080) — a square source needs no crop position at all, which is why
  card 1's photo (also natively square) never had this problem. If a future
  roster photo isn't square, crop it to square before import rather than
  reaching for Astro's `fit`/`position` props — this section already tried
  that path and it doesn't reliably work for this circular-avatar case.

  GOAL STATEMENT ADDED (2026-09-10, owner request). Sits between the section
  heading and the roster grid: "A Yin and Yang balance of at least 20 influencers
  with unique personas, voices, and messages." This is a target, not a
  headcount — phrased and placed to read as one (a labelled "Goal", separate
  from the roster list below it, not a fourth roster entry), consistent with
  REVIEW FIX 4's "no invented roster" rule: stating an intended future size is
  not the same as claiming 20 people exist or are in conversation. Reuses
  `.card`'s dashed placeholder border, which fits here too — a goal not yet
  met is exactly the "scaffolding, not finished" meaning that border exists
  to carry.

  APPLY CTA ADDED AFTER THE ROSTER GRID (2026-09-11, owner request). Roster is
  the last section on the page (index.astro), so this is the page's actual
  closing beat — see the render-order comment there on why that gap-as-ask
  framing is deliberate. `.cta-card` deliberately does NOT reuse `.card`'s
  dashed --border-placeholder: that border means "scaffolding, not finished"
  (tokens.css), and this card — real text, a real working button — is
  finished content, not an unfilled slot. Styled instead with the site's
  ordinary finished-surface pattern (--color-bg-elevated / --radius-md /
  --shadow-float, "cards float on shadow, not outline") that EventCard,
  CityCard, CommunityProof, and PitchVibe's own cards already use. Button is
  the exact same HeartSignalButton and label as the nav's primary CTA
  (Navigation.astro), one control reused rather than a second thing
  pretending to be the first — but its own target, not the nav's
  /#subscribe: it points at /influencer-application (2026-09-11), the real
  page that placeholder was standing in for until it existed.
*/

interface RosterEntry {
  name?: string;
  role?: string;
  url?: string;
  photo?: ImageMetadata;
  interested?: boolean;
}

// First two entries are confirmed real people (owner-supplied, 2026-09-10),
// each confirmed by the owner as having agreed to be named publicly in this
// funding-pitch context (the DATA GAP consent requirement below) — name,
// role, and a link to their own site. The rest stay role-only placeholders:
// the network's own language for what a person does, with no person
// attached. An invented name here would be the fabrication the whole section
// exists to avoid.
const roster: RosterEntry[] = [
  {
    name: 'Galactic Monk',
    role: 'Wayshower, Alchemist, & Producer',
    url: 'https://galacticmonk.com',
    photo: galacticMonkPhoto,
    interested: true,
  },
  {
    name: 'Sarah Starr',
    role: 'Galactic Guide, Space Weather, & Astrology',
    url: 'https://sarahstarrofficial.com',
    photo: sarahStarrPhoto,
    interested: true,
  },
  ...Array.from({ length: 18 }, (): RosterEntry => ({})),
];
---

<Section id="roster">
  <Container>
    <SectionHeader
      kicker="Current roster"
      heading="Influencer talent list to be updated as prospects verify interest."
      spacing="compact"
    />

    <div class="card goal">
      <p class="goal-label">Goal</p>
      <p class="goal-text">Reach out and gather a roster of at least 20 on-camera influencers with unique personas, voices, and messages.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="roster" role="list">
      {roster.map((person) => (
        <li class="card">
          {person.name ? (
            <>
              {person.photo && (
                <Image class="card-photo" src={person.photo} alt={person.name} width={160} height={160} loading="lazy" />
              )}
              {person.interested && (
                <span class="interest-badge">
                  <span class="interest-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  Interested
                </span>
              )}
              <h4 class="card-name">{person.name}</h4>
              <p class="card-role">{person.role}</p>
              {person.url && (
                <a
                  class="card-link"
                  href={person.url}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  aria-label={`${person.name}'s website`}
                >
                  <span class="card-link-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </a>
              )}
            </>
          ) : (
            <>
              <span class="pending-avatar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="pending-text">Slot pending</p>
            </>
          )}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="cta-card">
      <p class="cta-text">Interested in joining the influencer roster?</p>
      <HeartSignalButton href="/influencer-application">Influencer Application</HeartSignalButton>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Section>

<style>
  .card {
    /* The one sanctioned use of an outline on this site: an unfilled surface has
       to read as scaffolding rather than as a finished card. See
       --border-placeholder in tokens.css. */
    border: var(--border-placeholder);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    /* Positioning context for .interest-badge, which sits in the card's own
       top-right corner rather than on the avatar (see that rule for why). A
       no-op for every card without a badge, .goal included. */
    position: relative;
  }

  .pending-text {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .goal {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .goal-label {
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-electric-cyan);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .goal-text {
    color: var(--color-text-body);
  }

  /* Finished-content card, not scaffolding — see the header comment's APPLY
     CTA note on why this deliberately does not reuse `.card`. Same
     background/radius/shadow recipe as PitchVibe's own cards. */
  .cta-card {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-float);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-text {
    max-width: 40ch;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-text-body);
  }

  .card-role {
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-electric-cyan);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .roster {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .card-photo {
    display: block;
    width: var(--space-24);
    height: var(--space-24);
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Corner badge on the CARD, not the avatar (2026-09-10, owner request,
     iterated three times same-day). First try overlapped the 96px avatar
     circle — "Interested" plus an icon is roughly as wide as the avatar
     itself, so any corner placement on the circle either covered the face
     or hung off its edge. The card has real room instead: the photo sits at
     the card's top-left at its own fixed 96px width, leaving the top-right
     empty — but only barely, at the row's tightest point. At the 1100px
     five-up breakpoint the card is ~170px wide with --space-6 (24px)
     padding, so the photo's box (96px, starting at the content edge) ends
     24px from the card's top — the badge has to fit inside that 24px strip
     above it or it overlaps again, which is why the sizing below is
     measured in hard pixels instead of the space-N scale: nothing on that
     scale is small enough. Verified against the actual tightest card, not
     estimated. `.card` carries `position: relative` for this to anchor to.
     font-size 0.625rem matches CityCard.astro's own corner-badge precedent
     (also below any token) rather than inventing a different tiny size. */
  .interest-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: 6px;
    right: 8px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    font-family: var(--font-accent);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .interest-icon {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--color-electric-cyan);
    mask: url(/check.svg) center / contain no-repeat;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* Same circle footprint as .card-photo, so the unfilled slot lines up with
     the two real avatars beside it in the row instead of leaving a gap where
     a photo would go. The icon is a mask, not an <img>, so it takes a token
     fill instead of the baked-in one the source SVG ships with (see
     public/anon.svg — swapped in from question-mark.svg, 2026-09-10, owner
     request: a generic "anonymous person" glyph reads more like an avatar
     placeholder than a bare "?" does).

     Background is OfferingCard.astro's card gradient
     (`linear-gradient(45deg, #1a1a1a, #262626)`), copied verbatim rather than
     extracted to a shared token (2026-09-10, owner request, to visually match
     the offering cards). That gradient is pre-existing standards debt on this
     site — hard-coded hex, not tokens.css values — inherited as-is in
     OfferingCard.astro (see index.astro's import comment) rather than fixed;
     copying it here matches that debt intentionally, it does not introduce a
     new instance of it. If OfferingCard's gradient is ever tokenized, update
     this rule to match rather than leaving it pointing at stale hex. */
  .pending-avatar {
    display: block;
    position: relative;
    width: var(--space-24);
    height: var(--space-24);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: linear-gradient(45deg, #1a1a1a, #262626);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .pending-avatar::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: auto;
    width: 40%;
    height: 40%;
    background: var(--color-text-primary);
    mask: url(/anon.svg) center / contain no-repeat;
  }

  .card-name {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  /* Icon-only external link, replacing the plain-text domain (2026-09-10,
     owner request). `aria-label` on the <a> carries the accessible name
     since there's no visible text — "{name}'s website" rather than a bare
     "Website" so a screen-reader user landing here via the roster's link
     list still knows which card they're in. `display: inline-flex` rather
     than block, so the link's hit target is exactly the icon's box, not the
     full card width. */
  .card-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .card-link-icon {
    display: block;
    /* public/website.svg is drawn at 24x24 with fine detail (globe
       lat/long lines plus a small link-arrow overlay); at --space-4 (16px)
       that detail compressed into an indistinct blob (owner-reported,
       2026-09-10). --space-6 renders it at native size instead of shrinking
       it further. */
    width: var(--space-6);
    height: var(--space-6);
    background: var(--color-electric-cyan);
    mask: url(/website.svg) center / contain no-repeat;
  }

  /* FIVE-CARD ROW (2026-09-10, owner request) — up from three, to hold two
     named people plus three "Slot pending" cards without any of them
     wrapping to a second row on typical desktop widths. Three steps instead
     of the old two:

     - Below 640px: single column (unchanged).
     - 640–1099px: two columns, at the original --space-8 gap/padding — with
       five cards that's 3-then-2, not the old 3-card 2-then-1 split this
       file used to explicitly reject; an uneven last row reads as a roster
       still filling in, not as a mistake, once there are enough cards that a
       reader isn't consciously counting them.
     - 1100px+: all five across. This is where the padding and gap step down
       from --space-8 to --space-6 (see .card and this rule) — fitting five
       229px-ish columns at container-max (1440px) needs the room back that
       two wider gaps and eight extra padding-px per card side would cost.
       `minmax(0, 1fr)` rather than plain `1fr` on purpose: a bare `1fr`
       track won't shrink narrower than its content's min-content size, and
       this row's content includes a fixed 96px avatar — without the
       explicit `minmax(0, …)` floor, five of those could force the grid
       wider than the container instead of letting the surrounding text wrap
       first. */
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .roster {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    .roster {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }

    .card {
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
</style>
